# Brand

## Elements

- **Accueil lockup** — rasters cropped from mockup v3 (`/brand/accueil-mark.png`
  + `/brand/accueil-wordmark.png`). SVG cannot match the fused P+arrow+U and
  the U-stem italic wordmark at Accueil size. Tagline stays HTML (i18n):
  « Organiser. Compétiter. Progresser. »
- **Chrome lockup** — same Accueil mark (arrow is a real transparency, navy
  shows through) + `/brand/accueil-wordmark-on-chrome.png` (`Play` recolored
  to `--color-on-chrome`, `'Up` unchanged). Used in the rail via
  `PlayUpLockupMark` + `PlayUpWordmark surface="chrome"`. Collapsed rail =
  mark only. Phone: same lockup at the top of the overlay (above Pilotage),
  visible only when the menu is open.
- **Favicon** — same mark PNG (`/brand/accueil-mark.png`). No SVG monogram.
- **Wordmark** — `PlayUpWordmark` surfaces `home` and `chrome` only (PNG).
- **Arrow / "Up"** — lockup U-stem and `TrendIcon`. **Not** the rail current
  bar (straight 3px, Shell A).

## Angle system — **12° (arbitrated 2026-09-01)**

12° remains for `TrendIcon` and `--brand-skew` only.
**Not** the rail current indicator (straight bar, Shell A 2026-09-02).
**Not** a logo / wordmark skew — lockups are rasters.

Rationale: 12° survives better at small sizes (trends) and reads as a coherent
system. The Lab arbitration view (9° vs 12° on a typed wordmark) was retired
once the PNG lockup became SoT.

## Gradient

Allowed: Accueil lockup mark, Accueil `'Up` wordmark, Home atmosphere.
Never on buttons, body text, borders, badges, panels, page titles, or favicon
treatment beyond the mark raster itself.

## Forbidden

- Gradient on UI chrome/controls; mark as watermark; skewing tables/forms/panels.
- Brand blue as a status color.
- Italic wordmark as live type in chrome (rail uses the Accueil raster, not
  a skewed Plex span).
- A second logo pipeline (SVG monogram, typed wordmark, `leanDeg`).
